Since we PSBTv2 has been merged, do you think it is a good adition to add an rpc call that allows to add inputs and outputs in to an existing PSBT? Since PSBTv2 allows for the inputs and outputs to be modified I think it would be nice to let users do that through an RPC call.

  I've started to play around with this idea adding a new RPC method called `addinputspsbt` (probably not he best name). For now what I've done is that pssing an encoded PSBT and new input/s inside an array in one of these formtats: encoded PSBTInput or `[{\"txid\":\"myid\",\"vout\":0, \"sequence\":0}]`, it adds those inputs to the PSBT (you can see the code [here](https://github.com/Bicaru20/bitcoin/tree/2026-AddInput_outputs_psbt), the CI fails but this si just for you to see the idea of what I want to do).

<details>
<summary>
To ilustrate my implementation better, I have an example done in regtest:
</summary>

