My idea is to add to the same RPC method an option to also add the outputs, that way the user could choose if to add inputs, outputs or both of them. 

While making this implementation, I didn't understand the behaviour of the `PSBT_GLOBAL_TX_MODIFIABLE` flag. I don't get how the user has any say over its value, and therefore whether the PSBT's inputs and outputs can be modified. When I created the PSBT, this flag was set to `std::nullopt`. Why is this the default value? I understand that once the inputs are signed, whether they can still be modified depends on whether the signature sighash contains the `SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY`. But when creating a PSBT with no signatures yet, shouldn't it be possible to add more inputs by default? I'm missing something and I don't know what it is.

That being said, I just wanted to dicuss here if this is worth implementing and if the approach I proposed is the correct one.
